bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_inline_block_flex_percent_margin_item_1px_2026-11-27, 0, "Shrink-to-fit inline-block whose only content is display:flex with one 40x20 item at margin-left:10%: Chrome sizes the inline-block to the max-content 40px (% margin 0 in intrinsic sizing), then resolves 10% of 40 = 4px and the item shrinks to 36px."
    web_inline_block_flex_percent_margin_item_1px_2026-11-27, 1, "Chrome 159: k=1 44..79, k=4 176..319. Head (seed fb80903917d6d5f5): k=1 40..40, k=4 160..163 (item collapses to 1px at the container start). The float:left variant of the same tree matches Chrome (44..79 / 176..319), so the gap is in inline-block intrinsic width of a flex container."
    web_inline_block_flex_percent_margin_item_1px_2026-11-27, 2, "Minimal repro (body{margin:0}, .w{margin-left:40px;width:200px;height:30px}, 400x300, measure blue run on CSS row 10): <div class=\"w\" style=\"width:205px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"display:flex\"><div style=\"margin-left:10%;width:40px;height:20px;background:#00f\"></div></div></div></div>"

